review_comments.body:
Previously, it just returned -1 without initializing `*failure`. It still does the same if `PyObject_Str()` or `_copy_string_obj_raw()` fail.

Maybe initialize `*failure` unconditionally at the beginning of the function?

```suggestion
    *failure = (_PyXI_failure){
        .code = code,
        .msg = NULL,
        .msg_owned = 0,
    };
    if (obj == NULL) {
        return 0;
    }
```
